{%- comment -%}
  Search. Brief §5 puts a search mark in the header, beside Account and Cart.

  This route used to render main-stub, and the header carried no mark at all —
  header.liquid said so in as many words: "there is no search on the site yet,
  and an icon that does nothing is worse than one absence." The brief asked for
  search, so the absence is over and the mark in the header now has somewhere to
  go: it is a link to this page, not a panel that drops out of the bar.

  A LINK RATHER THAN AN OVERLAY, deliberately. An overlay is a second disclosure
  in a header that already has one, it needs its own focus trap and its own
  escape handling, and it cannot work with script off — so the fallback would be
  a magnifier that does nothing, which is the state the brief was asked to fix.
  A page has a URL, works with no JavaScript at all, is shareable, and puts the
  field at a size somebody can actually type a garment name into. If a
  type-ahead overlay is wanted later it enhances this page rather than replacing
  it.

  `type=product` is a hidden input rather than a query the merchant has to
  remember. Shopify searches pages and articles too, and this theme has neither
  designed: an unrestricted search would return a page card the theme has no
  markup for. Restricting it here keeps the results grid honest about what it can
  render.

  THREE STATES, and they are three different facts, so they do not share markup:
  nothing searched yet (the field and a prompt), searched with results (the
  grid), searched with none (the alert naming the terms back). The catalogue
  makes the same distinction between an empty collection and a collection
  filtered to nothing, and for the same reason — a shopper who mistyped needs to
  see what they typed.

  There is deliberately NO placeholder grid on the empty state. main-collection
  draws placeholder cards because "no products imported yet" is a fact about the
  store that the layout has to be reviewable against; here an empty state means
  the reader has not typed anything, and nine grey cards would answer a question
  nobody asked.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_sizes = '(min-width: 1280px) 22vw, (min-width: 640px) 40vw, 45vw'
-%}

{% paginate search.results by section.settings.per_page %}
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter pb-section pt-block-lg">
    <h1 class="text-h1 leading-h1">{{ 'search.title' | t }}</h1>

    <form action="{{ routes.search_url }}" method="get" role="search" class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <input type="hidden" name="type" value="product">

      <label class="sr-only" for="search-terms">{{ 'search.label' | t }}</label>
      {%- comment -%}
        `type="search"` gives the field its own clear affordance on the platforms
        that draw one, and `autocomplete="off"` keeps the browser's history of
        every other search box on the web out of a field about garment names.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input
        id="search-terms"
        type="search"
        name="q"
        value="{{ search.terms | escape }}"
        autocomplete="off"
        placeholder="{{ 'search.placeholder' | t }}"
        class="min-h-13 min-w-0 flex-1 basis-full rounded-sm border border-line bg-canvas px-4 text-body text-ink placeholder:text-ink-subtle sm:basis-auto"
      >

      {%- assign search_cta = 'search.submit' | t -%}
      {% render 'button', label: search_cta, variant: 'primary', type: 'submit', class: 'basis-full sm:basis-auto px-6 sm:px-11' %}
    </form>

    {%- if search.performed -%}
      <p class="mt-6 text-caption text-ink-muted">
        {{ 'search.results_count' | t: count: search.results_count, terms: search.terms }}
      </p>

      {%- if search.results.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="mt-block grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-4 gap-y-8 sm:gap-x-7 sm:gap-y-10 xl:grid-cols-3">
          {%- for item in search.results -%}
            <div data-reveal>
              {% render 'product-card', product: item, heading_level: 'h2', sizes: card_sizes %}
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        {% render 'pagination', paginate: paginate %}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign nothing = 'search.no_results' | t: terms: search.terms -%}
        <div class="mt-7">{% render 'alert', body: nothing %}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- else -%}
      <p class="mt-7 wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">{{ 'search.prompt' | t }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{% endpaginate %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Search",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Results are restricted to products. The theme has no card for a page or an article result, so returning one would render markup that does not exist." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "per_page", "label": "Results per page", "min": 6, "max": 24, "step": 3, "default": 9 }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
